  "final_answer_preview": "The act of forging a document to claim property falls under the definition of forgery as outlined in Section 336(1) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, which states that making a false document with intent to support a claim or cause someone to part with property constitutes forgery. The punishment for forgery is detailed in Section 336(2), which allows for imprisonment of up to two years, a fine, or both. If the forged document is a valuable security or similar, the penalties are more severe, as described in Section 338, which can lead to imprisonment for life or up to ten years, along with fines.",
